@prefix qa: <urn:sc-runtime:qa:> .

<urn:sc-runtime:qa:b-17:ARCH-B17-001>
  qa:id "ARCH-B17-001" ;
  qa:sprint "b-17" ;
  qa:qaPass "qa-b-17-1" ;
  qa:severity "Blocking" ;
  qa:status "fixed" ;
  qa:reviewer "arch-qa" ;
  qa:commit "a250fcf3144c1cf84ba8f7fbde81a520aad01ee0" ;
  qa:location "crates/sc-cron/src/worker/worker_runs.rs:330" ;
  qa:issue "Scheduled panic/join diagnostics bypass the occurrence redaction boundary. A registered Monty handler can panic with a reference/file/process value passed by source such as panic_host(os.getenv(\"KEY\")). monty_run.rs:184-207 moves the snapshot into the blocking feed and resumes the original panic unchanged. The worker extracts its raw &str/String at worker_runs.rs:539-545, writes it into feed.join_failed fields at :337-340, and persists it in FEED_JOIN_FAILED at :345. The due-run Monty join similarly inserts raw JoinError text into events and returned outcomes at scheduler/run_due.rs:524,533. A panicking EnvironmentReferenceResolver on a Python occurrence also reaches worker.rs:895-907 or the abortable due-run join at run_due.rs:500-505 with arbitrary provider panic text, including reference locators. ADR-RUN-0016 point6 (docs/architecture.md:2599-2610) requires hook/provider-controlled details to be redacted or value-free before diagnostics/outcomes/events/persistence and forbids emitted provider prose/locators. Accepted trusted-code panic/isolation risks do not authorize these library-owned copies of raw panic payloads. This is a source-traced failure path; no runtime witness was executed by this reviewer." ;
  qa:recommendation "Keep panic/join classification, fixed FEED_JOIN_FAILED/DUE_JOIN_FAILED/JOB_JOIN_FAILED codes, direct logger ownership, correlation, guards and cleanup intact, but use fixed value-free detail for environment-bearing hook/provider panic branches, or sanitize their payload while the private occurrence snapshot is still available before any outer JoinError formatting. Cover worker and run_due paths, including resolver panics, without changing the Rust Job interface or globally redacting fixed codes/recovery. Add focused canary checks for custom-handler and resolver panic text in scheduled events, returned/persisted outcomes; provider locators must remain absent. No public JobContext, logger wrapper, signing/sandbox feature, new provider or ADR relaxation is required." .
